{"ts": "2026-07-29T01:11:17", "session": "20260729-011010", "seq": 1, "kind": "note", "note": "verdict(headerleds): trials:\n\n  byte1        no\n  byte2        no\n  byte3        no\n  byte4        bottom left segment, middle part\n  byte5        bottom left segment, middle part slightly to the right\n  byte6        bottom left segment, middle part more to the right\n  byte7        bottom left segment, middle part more to the right\n  all 1..63    yes\n\nBytes 4, 5, 6, 7 light LEDs \u2014 they are pixel data, not header.\n\nThe data therefore starts at byte 4, giving 60 LEDs.\n\nThat explains both faults directly: byte 3 has been 0xd0 in all\nthree planes on every frame, which is (208,208,208) \u2014 the\npermanently white spot \u2014 and bytes 4..6 have been 0x00 in all\nthree, the permanently dark one.\n\nFix: DATA_FIRST = 4 in omenled/protocol.py, and shorten\nHEADER_TAIL to match.\n\nFull-brightness write: yes"}
